// W06 B12: Candidate recompute orchestrator (internal Worker export for Main B13 / B14).
// LOCAL try: buildComponents -> runComponentRaw for every row in physical row order (the actual W05 seen epoch returned
// by each call is passed to the next) -> no DIRTY Side left -> mergeSideRaw Support, then Resistance -> the W05 winner
// buffer is rebuilt from the merged records ([Support][Resistance], fields 0-13, reference price, root IDs in order with
// offsets rewritten to the new global root pool) after every check passed -> the global seen state is stamped with the
// W05 epoch advance (epoch += 1, seen array grown to the Root slot count with 0) for each Side with status >= 0, Support
// then Resistance, starting from the last component epoch. A cache-hit-only bar still re-materializes from the merge.
// Any structural failure (build fallback, run false, DIRTY left, merge false, capacity, seen identity) abandons LOCAL
// with nothing committed to the W05 buffers and runs fullFallbackRaw once, starting from the latest seen epoch token so
// no component seen stamp can be mistaken for the new scans; the W06 cache is then invalid (next ID = input, visit epoch
// 0 with the visited array zeroed, affected / removed cleared). A computed Side -1 is a LOCAL success.
// Returns the 31 W05 selectBothSides outputs (same order and types), then [nextComponentId, cacheValid,
